# W21 packaging — shared parameter documentation for the CP API.
#
# The `d/p/q/r/t***_cp` wrappers are generated by extendr from the Rust source
# (`src/rust/src/lib.rs`). Rather than repeat the same `@param` block on all 53
# functions, each wrapper inherits these definitions via `@inheritParams
# fitdistcp_params`. This file is hand-written (not generated) and is the single
# source of truth for the shared argument documentation.

#' Shared parameters for the fitdistcp CP functions
#'
#' Documentation for the arguments shared by the `d/p/q/r/t***_cp` functions.
#' These are not called directly; they are inherited by the model wrappers.
#'
#' @param x Numeric vector of observations (the data the model is fitted to).
#' @param y Numeric vector of prediction points at which the predictive
#'   density/CDF is evaluated.
#' @param p Numeric vector of probabilities in `[0, 1]` for the predictive
#'   quantile functions.
#' @param n Integer scalar: the number of random deviates to generate.
#' @param t Numeric vector of predictor (covariate) values for the `_p1`
#'   (predictor) models.
#' @param t0 Scalar prediction point for the `_p1` models. If supplied, `n0`
#'   must be absent.
#' @param n0 1-based positional index into `t` giving the prediction point
#'   (`t0 = t[n0]`), used when `t0` is not supplied.
#' @param _n,_x,_t,_t0,_n0 Placeholder arguments accepted by the `t***_cp`
#'   posterior-sampling wrappers for signature compatibility with the reference
#'   package. Posterior sampling is deferred to Phase 2, so these are unused.
#' @param method Placeholder argument accepted by `tgev_cp` for signature
#'   compatibility with the reference package (Phase 2).
#' @param a,b Numeric vectors of equal length (Phase 0 smoke-test helpers).
#' @param values Numeric vector (Phase 0 smoke-test helper).
#'
#' @details
#' The `t***_cp` posterior-sampling wrappers accept the same `n`, `x`, `t`,
#' `t0`, `n0` arguments as their `d/p/q/r` counterparts for signature
#' compatibility with the reference package, but posterior sampling is deferred
#' to Phase 2, so those arguments are currently unused.
#' @name fitdistcp_params
NULL
